KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ alias of a function type with a pack: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.typedef]/2, [temp.variadic]/5: for X<int, char>, `using F =
void(T...);' is void(int, char).  cpp_typecheckt::convert_parsed_parameters
leaves a function type with a pack expansion in parsed form, and assigning
cb to the F * member is a conversion error ("invalid implicit conversion
from 'auto (*)(signed int, char) -> void' to 'auto (*)(signed int) ->
void'").  `typedef void F(T...);' and non-pack aliases work
(cpp11_alias_declaration_of_function_type).  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
